  'apps/shopee/lib/shopee/fixtures/piiScan.ts':
    '`deepEqual` compares a committed Shopee wire body against its own re-redaction, so the fold decides "did redaction leave this leaf alone?" — the Shopee-shaped sibling of the Mercado Livre entry above. Equal: structural identity ONLY — same key SET (order-independent), same primitive values, `null` equal only to `null`. Distinct: a placeholder vs the value it replaced (that inequality IS the finding), `null` vs `"REDACTED"`, `0` vs `"0"`, arrays of different length, and — Shopee-specific — a MASKED value (`"****"`, `P******n`) vs a redacted one, because `redact.ts` keeps masked values verbatim and a fold that treated the two as the same would hide a leak sitting in a masked-looking field. ⚠️ The dangerous direction is folding too MUCH: a `deepEqual` that coerced types or ignored key order would report a leaked street address as "unchanged" and the corpus would ship it. Near-miss: `piiScan.test.ts` — "CONTROLE A (sabidamente ruim) — um corpo NÃO redigido reporta cada folha pessoal" (must differ) paired with "CONTROLE B (sabidamente bom) — o corpo redigido é ponto fixo e não reporta nada" (must not).',
  'apps/loja-integrada/lib/lojaIntegrada/fixtures/piiScan.ts':
    'TWO folds. (1) `deepEqual` compares a sanitized Loja Integrada fixture body (and its request line) against its own re-sanitization through the `fixture` profile, so the fold decides "did redaction leave this leaf alone?". Equal: structural identity ONLY — the same key SET (order ignored), the same primitive values, `null` equal only to `null`, arrays element by element. Distinct: a placeholder and the value it replaced (that inequality IS the finding), `null` vs `"REDACTED"`, `0` vs `"0"`, arrays of different length. ⚠️ The dangerous direction is folding too MUCH: a coercing or order-only fold would read a leaked value as unchanged and the sanitizer would write it. Near-miss: `piiScan.test.ts` — "CONTROL A (known-bad): an unredacted body is reported, path by path" (must differ) paired with "CONTROL B (known-good): the redaction of that body is a fixpoint and reports nothing" (must not). (2) `contemNomeDeLoja` matches the owner\'s local store-name list under `dobrarNomeDeLoja`: accents, case and any run of separators fold away, and a MULTI-word term also matches with its separators removed. The text is tried as written, percent-decoded (up to three rounds) and with every `%XX` escape dropped, because the redactor keeps a query value AS WRITTEN after testing it decoded. Folding more is the safe direction here (a match refuses the run), and a term never matches a different word. Equal: `Loja Exemplo` ≡ `LOJA EXÊMPLO` ≡ `loja-exemplo` ≡ `lojaexemplo` ≡ `LOJA%2FEXEMPLO` ≡ `LOJA%252FEXEMPLO`. Distinct: `Loja Exemplar` and `LOJA%2FEXEMPLAR`; a single-word term across two words (`mega` vs `time gap`). Near-miss: `piiScan.test.ts` — "a term matches its case and accent variants, and the same words with other separators" and "a term matches through percent-encoding (a kept query value stays as written)" paired with "a term does not match a different word" and "near-miss: percent-encoding never makes a different word match".',
  'apps/amazon/lib/amazon/fixtures/piiScan.ts':
    'TWO folds (the Amazon sibling of the Loja Integrada entry above). (1) `deepEqual` compares a sanitized Amazon fixture — its response body, its request body, its request line and its zip-entry names — against its own re-sanitization through the `fixture` profile, re-run with a faker that keeps ONLY values already in a fake format (`falsificadorDeVerificacao`), so the fold decides "did redaction leave this leaf alone?". Equal: structural identity ONLY — the same key SET (key ORDER is the one thing folded away), the same primitive values, `null` equal only to `null`, arrays element by element. Distinct: a placeholder or a fake and the value it replaced (that inequality IS the finding), one changed character, a changed JSON type, an extra key or array element. ⚠️ The dangerous direction is folding too MUCH: a coercing fold would read a leaked value as unchanged and the sanitizer would write it to a PUBLIC fixture. Near-miss: `piiScan.test.ts` — "CONTROL A (known-bad): a hand-edited fixture is reported as residue, path by path" (must differ) paired with "CONTROL B (known-good): every committed-shape fixture is a fixpoint and reports nothing" (must not), and "key ORDER alone is not residue" against "near-miss: one changed character, a type change and an extra element are residue". (2) `contemNomeDeLoja` matches the owner\'s local denylist under `dobrarNomeDeLoja`: accents, case and any run of separators fold away, and a MULTI-word term also matches with its separators removed; the text is tried as written, percent-decoded (up to three rounds) and with every `%XX` escape dropped. Folding more is the safe direction (a match refuses the run): the match is a SUBSTRING under the fold, deliberately inside a longer word too (`silva` in `silvana`, a store name glued into a host, SKU or e-mail local part), because a false refusal costs the owner a more specific term while a word-boundary miss publishes the name. Equal: `Termo Ficticio` ≡ `TERMO FICTÍCIO` ≡ `termo-ficticio` ≡ `termoficticio` ≡ `termo%20ficticio` ≡ `termo%2520ficticio`; and a term counts as found inside `silvana`, `lojaexemplostore.com`, `EXEMPLO123`. Distinct: text that differs from the term INSIDE it (`Termo Ficticia`, `exemplo` vs `exemplar`), and a single-word term across two words (`zeta` vs `ze ta`), so a term listed joined (`lojaexemplo`) misses the split name while one listed with its spaces (`loja exemplo`) finds both. Near-miss: `piiScan.test.ts` — "a term matches its case and accent variants, and the same words with other separators", "a term matches through percent-encoding, 1, 2 and 3 rounds" and "★ a term inside a longer word IS found (silva ⊂ silvana; a glued store name)" paired with "near-miss: a term does not match a word that differs from it inside", "near-miss: a word that differs from the term inside it is NOT found (exemplo vs exemplar)", "a term listed with its spaces finds the joined and the split name; near-miss: listed joined, it misses the split one" and "near-miss: percent-encoding never makes a different word match".',
